1. Using Kaye

   You may download Kaye from its official page, https://github.com/Toorium/Kaye,
   and use it for free, for any purpose, including paid work.

2. What you make is yours

   Animations, rigs, projects and any other files you make with Kaye belong to
   you. This license puts no limits on them.

3. Copying and changing

   You may copy Kaye and its source code onto your own devices, change the
   source code, and build your own versions, as long as you only use them
   yourself.

4. No distributing

   You may not share, sell, rent, upload, host or otherwise give anyone else a
   copy of Kaye, its source code, or a changed version of either, whether for
   free or for money. Two things are allowed:

   a. Linking to the official page above.
   b. Forking the repository on GitHub, as GitHub's terms allow, to send changes
      back through pull requests. A fork must keep this license, and must not
      publish builds or releases.

5. Sending changes back

   If you send a change to Kaye, for example through a pull request, you give
   Toorium permission to use, change and release it as part of Kaye, under this
   license or any other.

6. Keep this notice

   Any copy you are allowed to make must include this license and the copyright
   line above.

7. Other people's parts

   Kaye includes parts made by others, such as the Phosphor icons and Rust
   libraries. Those parts keep their own licenses, which come first for them.

8. No warranty

   Kaye is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied,
   including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose
   and noninfringement. In no event shall Toorium or anyone who contributed to
   Kaye be liable for any claim, damages or other liability, whether in
   contract, tort or otherwise, arising from, out of or in connection with Kaye
   or its use.

9. Ending

   If you break this license, your permission to use, copy and change Kaye
   ends.

10. Older versions

   Kaye 0.1.4 and earlier were released under the BSD 3-Clause License. Copies
   of those versions stay under that license. This license covers every
   version after them.

